direction: down
title: "HOOK ADMISSION AND COMPLETION GUARD\nActual target custody survives local ERROR and reset"
title.shape: text
entry: "Trace/dispatcher dependency registered before callouts\nPreserve source busy/suppression timing\nBind target lifetime, actual depth and entry kind"
hook: "Pre-readiness native hook can be called\nfreeProc / type cleanup / legacy variable traces\nSignature is not permission for arbitrary eval or reset"
admit: "HookAdmission\nOwner + object/target lifetime + allowed effects\nReentry / exit / depth floor + reset authority"
source: "Source reset event\nRecord actual predicate and before/after U\nCannot issue owned-completion authority"
owned: "Owned reset request\nValidate ancestor trace / native / generation frontier\nMissing authority: retain custody, deny reuse"
child: "Callback evaluation may finish locally\nNo waiting backward for its enclosing dispatcher\nOutstanding target custody remains with control owner"
late: "Actual trace restore + cleanup + dispatcher return\nRelease only the corresponding dependency\nParent final guard still validates whole target frontier"
warn: "Premature child clear + old saved U=1\nCan INTRODUCE resurrection during migration\nNot an implemented or observed legacy result"
entry -> hook -> admit
admit -> source -> child
admit -> owned -> child
child -> late
owned -> warn: "invalid shortcut"
hook.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
admit.style.fill: "#DFEEFF"
warn.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
late.style.fill: "#E8F4E8"
